  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You have NNN tasks, indexed 111 to NNN, where the iii-th of which takes AiA_iAi​ time to be completed by a skilled worker, and can be started only after the time SiS_iSi​ (including exactly at SiS_iSi​).\n\nYou have MMM workers, indexed 111 to MMM, where the iii-th of which has a skill deficiency factor of FiF_iFi​ meaning that if a skilled worker would take ttt time to complete the task, this worker will take Fi⋅tF_i \\cdot tFi​⋅t time.\n\nSuppose PiP_iPi​ is the worker assigned to task iii (1≤i≤N1 \\le i \\le N1≤i≤N). We require that PPP is a non-decreasing sequence, i.e. Pi≥Pi−1P_i \\ge P_{i - 1}Pi​≥Pi−1​.\n\nFind the earliest possible time where we can complete all the required tasks.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line contains NNN and MMM - the number of tasks and the number of workers\nThe second line contains NNN integers - A1,A2,....,ANA_1, A_2, ...., A_NA1​,A2​,....,AN​ : time required for a skilled worker to complete the iii-th task.\nThe third line contains NNN integers - S1,S2,....,SNS_1, S_2, ...., S_NS1​,S2​,....,SN​ : minimum possible starting time for the iii-th task.\nThe fourth line contains MMM integers - F1,F2,...,FMF_1, F_2, ..., F_MF1​,F2​,...,FM​ : skill deficiency factor of the iii-th worker.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the minimum possible time when all tasks are completed.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1041 \\le T \\le 10^41≤T≤104",
      "1≤N,M≤1051 \\le N, M \\le 10^51≤N,M≤105",
      "1≤Si,Ai≤N1 \\le S_i, A_i \\le N1≤Si​,Ai​≤N",
      "1≤Fi≤101 \\le F_i \\le 101≤Fi​≤10",
      "The sum of NNN and the sum of MMM over all test cases does not exceed 10510^5105"
    ],
